From c6550da04c20e8f20a53d101cc44bed853b0a325 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:55:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: send ordinary data frames without a fixed rate

Every data frame is sent with the descriptor's fixed-rate bit set and
the rate word naming OFDM 6 Mbit/s, so the air-time ceiling is 6 Mbit/s
whatever the link quality. The earlier attempt to lift this (proposal
0242, retired) cleared the fixed-rate bit but left the rate code in the
rate word, a form the vendor data path never produces: its data frames
carry no fixed-rate option at all, and its fixed rate is set only for
management frames at the BSS basic rate. Every data frame on that boot
completed with status 3, which therefore measured a malformed descriptor
rather than the firmware's rate adaptation.

Build ordinary data descriptors the way the vendor path does: no
fixed-rate bit, zero power offset, and the rate word left zero, so the
firmware selects the rate from the station record's rate set that
mac80211 supplied at association. Management and security frames keep
their fixed basic-rate descriptors. The TX-done event's rate field,
already parsed and logged, is the measurement. If data still completes
with status 3, the block is in what the firmware derives from the
station record, not in the descriptor.

Compile-tested in the development VM, strict checkpatch clean. Not yet
run on the device; one variable for one boot.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h
index f4dcc5268..3334d74d7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/join-tx.h
@@ -158,10 +158,14 @@ mt6797_join_tx_data_descriptor(const unsigned char *frame, size_t bytes,
 	d[6] = 0x80; /* Protected frame, TID 0, no header padding. */
 	d[7] = 1U << 2; /* Own-MAC 1. */
 	d[10] = lifetime;
-	d[11] = 0x80; /* Fixed rate enabled, zero power offset. */
+	/* No fixed rate, zero power offset, and the rate word (bytes 24-27)
+	 * left zero: an ordinary data frame takes the firmware's rate selection
+	 * over the station record's rate set. Management and security frames
+	 * keep their fixed basic-rate descriptors above.
+	 */
+	d[11] = 0;
 	d[12] = count; d[13] = count >> 8;
 	d[20] = pid; d[21] = 2; /* TX status to MCU. */
-	d[26] = (0x4bU << 2) & 255; d[27] = (0x4bU << 2) >> 8;
 	for (i = 0; i < MT6797_JOIN_TX_DESC_BYTES; i++)
 		output[i] = d[i];
 	*pages = (total + 127U) / 128U;
-- 
